                    },
                    "message": "Can you elaborate more on why these APIs are required, and who will be consuming this APIs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "updated commit message for use case and consumers"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "please review"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rashidmp",
                        "email": "rashidmp@ami.com",
                        "username": "rashidmp2002"
                    },
                    "message": "Could you explain the exact use case for this approach?\u200b\u200c\n\nAlso, the IP set via `SIOCSIFADDR` ioctl is only applied in the kernel at runtime and is not persisted anywhere. It will be lost after a reboot, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "In phosphor-networkd, interfaces listed in the IGNORED_INTERFACES\n environment variable are not exposed as DBus objects, and therefore\n will not appear in Redfish or WebUI.\n These interfaces may still require runtime IP configuration for\n BMC communication, even though external management\n is not needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Asmitha Karunanithi",
                        "email": "asmitk01@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "asmithakarun"
                    },
                    "message": "> Despite being ignored for external management, these interfaces still require `runtime IP configuration` for reliable BMC communication. Since no DBus objects exist for ignored interfaces, we use direct ioctl ystem calls to configure them.\n\nPlease highlight \"runtime config\" in the commit message"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
